\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar/yen rises, tries to sustain gains above 122. \b0\par\par\uc2 191 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1999\par 09:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  0735 GMT - Yen falls back. Dollar/yen makes foray above 122 but yet to sustain gains, euro/yen probes back above 126. Market wary of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after rhetoric overnight. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF's Sakakibara said weaker yen acceptable if needed for recovery, FinMin Miyazawa said recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at pre-empting unjustified yen rise, not boosting economic growth. \par \par \uc2  * South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy dollars. South Korea Finance Ministry official had overnight expressed concern about the won's strength vs yen and said was closely watching dlr/yen impact on local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  * Dollar/yen seen capped at 122.50/55. \par \par \uc2  * Euro above $1.03 after Mon's drop of nearly a cent. \par \par \uc2  * French April industrial output down a larger-than-expected 0.6 pct m/m but March figures revised up. Italy jobless rate falls to lower-than-expected 12.1 pct in April \par \par \uc2  * Bank of France's Trichet speaks on euro at 1630 GMT. \par \par \uc2  * U.K. Chancellor of Exchequer Brown attends House of Lords committee hearing on MPC at 1445 GMT. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6m06050\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
