\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Strong Asians leave yen behind. \b0\par\par\uc2 988 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1999\par 13:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 22 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah, South Korean won and Thai baht shone again on Tuesday as investors continued piling into Asian recovery stories, with dollar/yen relegated to a background factor. \par \par \uc2  Major Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a touch easier, pausing for breath after their recent ascent, but analysts said the Polish zloty looked set to push higher in the short term. \par \par \uc2  South Africa's rand firmed back through 6.0 to the dollar as Monday's positive data on gross domestic product offset the expected cut of one percentage point in bank prime rates. \par \par \uc2  Slightly weaker dollar/yen lent a mildly firmer flavour to emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed out of the market after recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  But some \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  streaked ahead. \par \par \uc2  "You get the feeling the markets are chasing the success stories - the baht and Korea for doing okay and the rupiah for not collapsing," said one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at a U.S. bank in London. \par \par \uc2  In less than three weeks the rupiah has surged from over 8,100 to the dollar to smash thorugh the 7,000 barrier, riding a wave of optimism over this month's peaceful general election. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts suggested the break above 7,000 could prove fragile, driven by rumours that the party leading the polls, the opposition Indonesia Democratic Party-Struggle (PDI-P), will adopt a fixed exchange rate regime. \par \par \uc2  But others said this was unlikely as PDI-P officials have said they would not fix the rate without International Monetary Fund approval, which was unlikely to be forthcoming. \par \par \uc2  They said a bigger problem could be an overshoot towards 6,000, causing export problems and fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility. \par \par \uc2  "The market is very relaxed about holding rupiah," said Gerry Celaya, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  technical analyst at American Express Bank in London, who saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushing on towards 6,600-6,500 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "People are still being squeezed out of long dollar positions that they had for the elections, and they're getting pummelled." \par \par \uc2  The won also firmed against both the dollar and the yen, despite renewed Bank of Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars, while the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted on a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comment that it would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to restrain baht strength. \par \par \uc2  The won could head for 1,120 to the dollar if the Bank of Korea let it slip convincingly through 1,160, one analyst said, while the baht could be headed for 36.00 or even the highs of around 35.60 seen late last year. \par \par \uc2  In Europe the Czech crown slipped slightly against the euro after GDP data showed the economy shrank by 4.5 percent year-on-year in the first quarter of 1999, worse than market expectations of a 3.3 percent decline. \par \par \uc2  The poor figure fanned expectations that the Czech National Bank will trim its benchmark two-week repo rate by between 10 and 40 basis points at its board meeting on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The zloty pulled back slightly from Monday's four-month high of 4.91 percent above its basket parity, but analysts said it would continue to be buoyed by expected privatisation inflows in the coming months. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was quoted around 4.68 percent above parity by mid-morning in London, could soon test 5.0 percent above parity. \par \par \uc2  The rand made a strong showing against the dollar after some initial profit-taking, cheered by revised GDP figures which showed the economy did not slip into recession last year and grew slightly in the first quarter of 1999. \par \par \uc2  The new accounting method, in line with international standards, also had the knock-on effect of improving key ratios such as the budget and current account deficits to GDP. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the much-awaited cut in the banks' prime rate on Monday, to 18 percent, was long overdue. ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates, including the change versus late New York trade the previous day and the change in the year to date.. ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , formerly quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to reflect new market norms. All other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are quoted against the dollar. ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the rise or fall of the dollar or euro value. ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the first day of the current trading year, January 4. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab     LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par CLOSE\tab \tab in 1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Czech Rep.\tab \tab     36.83   36.80   0.07%    5.83%\par Poland\tab \tab \tab    4.05    4.03   0.34%   -0.58%\par Hungary\tab \tab \tab 249.23  249.18   0.02%   -0.78%\par Slovakia\tab \tab 