\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar, euro rest near lows versus yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 190 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1999\par 13:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  1140 GMT - Nervous dollar, euro, hover above lows vs yen, well above Monday lows. But market wary of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after rhetoric overnight. Euro/dollar weaker in range. EU Commission says Italy inflation "in itself" not major worrying factor, treaty clear on "irrevocable nature of monetary union" after EU Prodi comments on Italy hit euro Monday. \par \par \uc2  * German FinMin sees signs of recovery growing, expects to hit 1999 growth forecast. \par \par \uc2  * Sterling gains after UK's Byers says in CNN interview sees euro membership "a few years off yet", UK unlikely to meet economic tests for euro entry until 2001 at earliest. \par \par \uc2  * MOF's Sakakibara said weaker yen acceptable if needed for recovery. \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  FinMin Miyazawa said recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at pre-empting unjustified yen rise, not boosting economic growth. \par \par \uc2  * South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy dollars. South Korea Finance Ministry official had overnight expressed concern about the won's strength vs yen and said was closely watching dlr/yen impact on local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  * Bank of France's Trichet speaks on euro at 1630 GMT. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6m05x9b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
