\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Dollar/yen soft, jumpy on BOJ fears. \b0\par\par\uc2 585 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 1999\par 10:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 22 (Reuters) - The dollar eased towards the lower end of the day's tight range in early European trading on Tuesday after a brief pop-up as the market remained extremely nervous about Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The short-lived rally came as the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars for won in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but it subsided as London traders saw no signs the BOJ had stepped in. \par \par \uc2  "When they (the BOJ) push it higher, it goes higher. But when they don't, it goes lower," Cameron Crise, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Warburg Dillon Read in London. "The question is, how long does it take for the market to start trying to push it lower." \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 121.89/99 yen at 0755 GMT after jumping above 122 for a few minutes from the day's low near 121.80. It had risen to a high of 122.51 overnight from 122.14/24 in Monday's late European session. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the 122.50 area was becoming strong resistance as the dollar had stalled there several times recently. \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, raw memories of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the previous two trading days limited the dollar's pullbacks. \par \par \uc2  "Anybody short of euro/yen, euro/dollar or dollar/yen lost a lot of money that day," a dealer at a European bank in London said. "Obviously people are going to be very nervous." \par \par \uc2  A Japanese bank dealer said the market was jumpy because there was no knowing whether the dollar's rally would stop at 122.50 yen the next time the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "If we break above 122.50, there will be a lot of stop-loss buying," he said. "So if you're short, you want to get out before we get there, as quickly as possible." \par \par \uc2  Overnight, Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said recent BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been aimed at pre-empting an unjustified, sharp yen rise, not at boosting economic growth. BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami said Japan's near-zero interest rate policy was starting to affect the economy. \par \par \uc2  The euro was stable, consolidating after Monday's losses on comments by European Commission President-designate Romano Prodi about Italy's place in European economic and monetary union. \par \par \uc2  Prodi later on Monday clarified his remarks, saying there was no risk of Italy leaving the euro. \par \par \uc2  The euro stood at $1.0332/36 at 0810 GMT, marginally above $1.0320/25 late in Monday's European trading. \par \par \uc2  France's industrial output was down 0.6 percent in April, with manufacturing output down 0.7 percent, while March data were revised higher. The numbers had little effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Bank of France Governor Jean-Claude Trichet speaks on the euro in Geneva at 1630 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Sterling backed off from its lows agains the dollar but softened against the euro, with a lack of domestic economic data leaving the market looking to euro/dollar for direction. \par \par \uc2  The pound stood at $1.5861/71 at 0835 GMT, up from a low of $1.5857 but slightly off $1.5882/87 late on Monday. Euro/sterling was at 65.12/17 pence from Monday's 64.98/01. \par \par \uc2  UK Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown gives evidence to a House of Lords committee on the Bank of England's Monetary Policy Committee at 1445 GMT. ((Shin Kishima, London Capital Markets +44-171-542-6721)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6m05whg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
