\par\par \b \uc2  Tokyo Afternoon Stocks Ease A Bit But Still At '99 Record \b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 1999\par 06:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Tokyo stocks remain at their strongest so far this year Monday afternoon, but prices are down a bit from midday as investors focus on profit-taking opportunities. \par \par \uc2  "We are seeing similar pattern to Friday, with strong foreign buying in the morning followed by selling pressure in the afternoon," said Darrel Whitten, a strategist at ABN AMRO. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 0408 GMT (12:08 a.m. EDT), the Nikkei average of 225 selected\par issues was up 218.88 points from Friday at 17650.14. That leaves it down\par somewhat from its morning close of 17713.21, the intraday high and a\par 1999 record.\par    The near-term September Nikkei futures contract was 180 points\par higher at 17670.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overseas institutional investors have continued to raise their\par weighting in Tokyo stocks on hopes that the Japanese economy has finally\par bottomed out, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There are also vague hopes for fresh economic stimulus measures after\par the Group of Seven nations over the weekend maintained pressure on Japan\par to do more to put its economy on a path of domestic demand-led growth.\par Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi in turn said that the Japanese government\par will take every measure available to ensure stable growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Stocks of big exporters and high-tech issues have been helped by a\par weaker yen Monday, as the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets again this session.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Participants generally expect the market to ease lower for the rest of\par the day.\par -by Ian Messer; 813-5255-2929; imesser@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-06-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0416GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  5011 55117 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6l04nnu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
