\par\par \b \uc2  Japan/Trade/Dips -2: Yen Stronger Vs Levels Last Year \b0\par\par\uc2 412 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 1999\par 05:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Soon after the data were released, the dollar shot up against the yen, propelled higher by another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's rise. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  eventually touched an intraday high of Y122.52, almost two yen higher than its early morning lows. \par \par \uc2  With the foundations of a recovery still wobbly, Japanese monetary officials have been adamant in their stand to prevent a "premature" appreciation of the yen, which they say could threaten to derail the economy. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, the dollar remains substantially weaker than it was a year ago, when it traded around Y140. \par \par \uc2  The euro has also lost ground against the yen over recent months, helping to constrict shipments of Japanese goods to European countries. The euro fell to around Y123.00 last Friday, down from around Y134 when it began trading in January. \par \par \uc2  Reflecting alarm over that development, the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday via the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro against the yen for the first time ever. \par \par \uc2  Despite large amounts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last 10 days, the yen remains stronger compared with levels a year ago. As a result, Japanese exports to Europe and the U.S. are likely to remain weak for the time being. \par \par \uc2  In May, exports to Europe plunged 17.5% from a year earlier - a stark contrast to the double-digit increases for much of last year. The pace of decline accelerated from a 7.8% fall in April and 3.5% decline in March. \par \par \uc2  Economists said that much of the reason for declining exports to Europe is due to stagnant demand there. \par \par \uc2  Further on, the outlook is brighter. With economic activity in Europe expected to rebound later this year, the trend will reverse, helping to provide support for overall Japanese exports, economists said. \par \par \uc2  "The pace of shrinkage in Japan's surplus will slow in response of rising exports to Europe" as economic growth there increases, Yoshino said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, as economic growth in Asia gathers momentum, exports to the region will also turn positive, analysts said. Exports to Asia fell 7.0% in May from a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  "I expect exports to Asia will recover in the second half of the fiscal year (ending March 2000), helping the trade surplus to regain positive growth," Yamazaki said. \par \par \uc2  -By Arran Scott (813-5255-2929; amscott@ap.org) \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 21-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0327GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6l04njp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
