\par\par \b \uc2  Buba's Welteke says ECB interested in strong euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 1999\par 11:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT, June 21 (Reuters) - Bundesbank president-designate Ernst Welteke said on Monday that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , like all central banks, was interested in a strong external value for its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and predicted that the euro's exchange rate would stabilise. \par \par \uc2  Welteke said last Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the ECB on behalf of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been in the spirit of international cooperation. \par \par \uc2  Speaking at a financial markets conference in Frankfurt, Welteke also said that he did not think \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a rule had any effect if it was pursued against the trend of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  "I am convinced that if a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meets a request for mutual support it serves a financial centre and international cooperation and I think that in this case it was correct," Welteke said referring to Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Welteke also said that the ECB's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  action on Friday did not imply that it had any material interest in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "If the ECB is asked by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for reasons it deems necessary, it is natural that it will do so," he said. \par \par \uc2  He added: "The ECB like all central banks is interested in a strong external value of the euro." \par \par \uc2  Welteke said the main reason for the euro's decline had been interest rate differentials between the United States and Europe and that those differentials were likely to diminish as Europe and the U.S. economies moved back in synch. \par \par \uc2  "I expect that the economy in Europe and the United States will in time, and I cannot give a time frame, run at the same speed, this will reduce interest rate differentials and the exchange rate will become more stable and closer to normal conditions," he said. ((David Crossland, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525, frankfurt.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6l063dm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
