\par\par \b \uc2  Yen can fall more if needed for economy-Sakakibara. \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 1999\par 12:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 21 (Reuters) - Japanese Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Eisuke Sakakibara said on Monday that Japan was ready to accept a weaker yen if necessary to help the economy recover. \par \par \uc2  "Further weakening of the yen is possible if it is necessary for the economy... We are flexible on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Sakakibara told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "What is of paramount importance is to ensure Japan's economic recovery as soon as possible," he said. \par \par \uc2  To achieve that goal, the Japanese monetary authorities may take decisive actions again to stem premature strengthening of the yen. \par \par \uc2  Referring to his remarks earlier on Monday that Japanese authorities neither intend to contain \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates within a narrow range nor plan any target zones, Sakakibara said this means that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has not been carried out with specific ranges in mind, but has been made on the basis of economic conditions at the time a policy decision is made. \par \par \uc2  "At this point, preventing a premature rise in the yen is important for the economy," he added. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara said Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the euro against the yen was the first time that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Europe through the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB). \par \par \uc2  "The ECB was quite efficient," Sakakibara said. "I am very grateful to the ECB and European authorities (for their cooperation)." \par \par \uc2  With this action, a tripolar \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime has been established for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary and the authorities in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the United states and Europe will closely monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates and cooperate with each other, he said. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the euro/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also partly aimed at helping Japanese investors suffering losses on euro-denominated investments, Sakakibara said it was not aimed at specific investors. \par \par \uc2  He quoted Japanese Vice Finance Minister Koji Tanami as saying that the Japanese authorities took appropriate actions on Monday but Sakakibara did not make it clear whether the ECB bought euro for yen on behalf of the BOJ again on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara added that the Japanese authorities will always monitor yen/dollar and yen/euro rates with interest. ((Tatsuo Ito, Tokyo News Room +813-3432-1396 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6l063d5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
