\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Shrugging off yen, watching Fed. \b0\par\par\uc2 874 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 1999\par 12:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 21 (Reuters) - Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were relatively quiet on Monday despite the yen's gyrations, with players waiting for the U.S. Federal Reserve to show its hand on interest rates when it meets next week. \par \par \uc2  Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were little changed, shrugging off renewed, aggressive Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which drove the dollar as high as 122.55 yen from around 120.70. \par \par \uc2  Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also range-bound, although dealers said better-than-expected Czech trade data nudged the crown higher against both the dollar and the euro despite continued talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is overvalued. \par \par \uc2  "They're relatively small moves. People either have positions on or they're sitting on their hands waiting for the Fed," said Callum Henderson, emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank in London. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah forged ahead once more to fresh eight-month highs, testing resistance at 7,000 to the dollar as post-election optimism was compounded by upbeat comments by a top International Monetary Fund official. \par \par \uc2  Visiting Jakarta on Friday, IMF first deputy managing director Stanley Fischer said the rupiah was still undervalued around 7,250 to the dollar and had further room to strengthen. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could speed on towards 6,500 to the dollar if it broke convincingly through the 7,000 barrier. \par \par \uc2  It failed to break 7,000 last week after chief economics minister Ginandjar Kartasasmita said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains were too rapid. But \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and IMF officials have since said a firmer rupiah would not hurt exports. \par \par \uc2  Most other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  softened slightly against the dollar, but less dramatically than the yen, leaving them stronger against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain trapped between a Bank of Japan adamant to prevent yen strength and better economic indicators attracting inflows into their equity markets," analysts at Standard Chartered said in a note to clients. \par \par \uc2  In Europe the Czech crown ticked up on data showing the country's trade gap narrowed sharply in May to 864 million crowns ($24.25 million), roughly one-tenth of the May 1998 deficit and hugely lower than market expectations. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said they expected gross domestic product figures on Tuesday to show further economic contraction in the first quarter of 1999, providing further ammunition for the Czech National Bank to cut interest rates by between 10 and 40 basis points at this week's policy meeting. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty was quoted around 4.6 percent above its basket parity, steady within what dealers see as a 4.4-5.0 percent range, as the market continued to await privatisation inflows. \par \par \uc2  A member of Poland's Monetary Policy Council, Dariusz Rosati, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's firming in recent weeks was probably led by small zloty purchases by Unicredito Italiano  to pay for its $1 billion purchase of local bank Pekao . \par \par \uc2  But he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  impact of the sale would be limited as Unicredito would meet over half the cost of its purchase through local credit. Rosati said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not concerned about the zloty's rise to current levels, although it would be happy to see privatisation inflows spread over time to defuse further upward pressure. ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates, including the change versus late New York trade the previous day and the change in the year to date.. ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , formerly quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to reflect new market norms. All other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are quoted against the dollar. ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the rise or fall of the dollar or euro value. ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the first day of the current trading year, January 4. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab     LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   CLOSE\tab \tab in 1999\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUROPE/MEAST/AFRICA\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Czech Rep.\tab \tab     36.88   36.93   -0.14%   5.96%\par  Poland\tab \tab \tab    4.05    4.06   -0.28%  -0.60%\par  Hungary\tab \tab \tab 249.31  249.57   -0.10%  -0.75%\par  Slovakia\tab \tab \tab 45.35   45.30    0.10%   5.46%\par  Romania\tab \tab \tab 15,775  15,780   -0.03%  44.06%\par  Ukraine\tab \tab \tab   3.98    3.98    0.05%   1.32%\par  South Africa\tab \tab    5.98    5.99   -0.13%   2.34%\par  Kenya\tab \tab \tab    74.00   74.25   -0.34%  20.13%\par  Israel\tab \tab \tab   4.081   4.064    0.42%  -0.92%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par LATAM\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Mexico\tab \tab \tab    9.35    9.37   -0.21%  -5.03%\par  Brazil\tab \tab \tab  1.7580  1.7580    0.00%  4