\par\par \b \uc2  Euro hits three-week highs vs yen, rises vs dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 219 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 1999\par 10:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 21 (Reuters) - The euro rose to three-week highs against the yen and gained more than a third of a cent against the dollar on Monday as traders in Tokyo said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was once again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen strength. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on market talk that it was buying euros for yen on behalf of the Bank of Japan, which had already been buying dollars for yen on its own account intermittently throughout the Asian session. \par \par \uc2  While dealers in Tokyo said the ECB was buying euros for yen on behalf of the Bank of Japan, traders in London who had dealt with European central banks on Friday played down such talk. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose as high as 127.35 yen, the strongest it has been since May 31 and climbed to $1.0420 by 0807 GMT. That compares with 124.84/03 and $1.0368/78 late in Europe on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 122.16/22, compared to the three-week high of 122.55 hit in Asia and 120.44 at the close of European trading on Friday. \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6l0623l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
