\par\par \b \uc2  Euro seen weak vs yen in Tokyo on Japanese selling. \b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 1999\par 02:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 21 (Reuters) - The euro is seen vulnerable to selling by Japanese investors and exporters in Tokyo on Monday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (BOJ) surprising \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday boosted the European unit by more than three yen. \par \par \uc2  But traders said it may be well underpinned above 123 yen as the BOJ hit the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market below that level on Friday with its third bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in less than two weeks, using the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) to sell yen for euro to curb the strength of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The ECB on Friday confirmed it had done so. It was the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since mid-1998. \par \par \uc2  The euro leaped to around 125.85 yen from a lifetime low of around 122.60 yen while the dollar rose nearly two yen from a session low of 119.00 yen after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 125.19/34 yen at 2327 GMT, little changed from around 125.18 yen in late New York on Friday, and the dollar was at 120.60/70 yen, compared with 120.30/45 yen. \par \par \uc2  Traders said chances of the BOJ buying dollars for yen in Tokyo may keep the U.S. unit's downside limited around 119 yen. \par \par \uc2  "We couldn't try the dollar's floor below 119 yen last week and we won't do so this week either," said a city bank trader. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ sold the yen for euro through the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday for the first time since the euro was launched in January. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came as the world's most powerful nations were meeting in Cologne and as bilateral talks between German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder and Obuchi were taking place. \par \par \uc2  Asking about rumours of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Haruhiko Kuroda, director-general of International Bureau of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  who is accompanying Obuchi to the summit, said: "It was a fact that we acted in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets today (Friday)." \par \par \uc2  Kuroda said: "Big fluctuations in (the Japanese) \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are unfavourable particularly at a time when the economy is in quite a sensitive stage before embarking on a full-fledged recovery." \par \par \uc2  A strong yen in theory undermines competitiveness of Japanese products on the overseas markets and hurts exporters' incomes, which could in turn throw cold water on Tokyo's policy steps. ((Risa Maeda, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-3432-8570 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6l0622l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
