\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr shoved higher as BOJ goes all out against yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 710 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 1999\par 06:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 21 (Reuters) - The dollar was shoved higher on Monday, gaining almost two yen to reach a three-week high against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to suppress the yen. In a show of brute force, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars in waves from 120.70 yen to a high of 122.55, spending a rumoured $5.0 billion or more in the process. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's persistence - this was the fourth burst of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 11 days - was reinforced by comments from senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Eisuke Sakakibara that the MOF did not mean to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in a narrow band. By 0300 GMT the dollar was up at 122.16/19 from an early 120.65/70. \par \par \uc2  Traders said this was an unusually explicit comment from Sakakibara, considered the key policy maker on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the MOF, and suggested the ministry would be happy to see the yen weaken a lot further from here. \par \par \uc2  If so, this would be a considerable shift in official policy which has generally favoured a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the long run, they said. \par \par \uc2  "It shows just how concerned the authorities are that the economic recovery here is not established, and that a higher yen would kill it stone dead, like so many before," said a senior trader at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  The markets have been moving to price in an economic recovery in Japan since January-to-March gross domestic product data released on June 10 showed a stunning 1.9 percent quarterly rise. The authorities have gone to great lengths to play down the figures, but analysts say offshore investors are afraid of missing the boat in Japan and are scrambling to pick up what many perceive to be cheap assets. \par \par \uc2  This has seen a flood of funds into Japanese equities, driving the Nikkei up over a thousand points or 6.6 percent since the GDP data. The rush of incoming funds has made it hard for the BOJ, since offshore investors needed yen to pay for these shares. \par \par \uc2  Analysts noted that the impact of the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be reduced if the BOJ sterilises it by draining the excess liquidity it generated out of the money market. \par \par \uc2  That was what it did with last Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , disappointing yen bears who had thought it might leave the liquidity in the market and so signal a looser policy stance akin to a quantitative easing. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market would be watching money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday and Wednesday, when the liquidity from Friday and Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should show up, but few thought the conservative \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would sanction such an easing. \par \par \uc2  Another burden for the BOJ is that many Japanese investors still have a lot of hedging to do on their holdings of euro debt, much of which was built up last year at average rates against the euro of well above 130.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  Many believe the BOJ's actions, most notably on Friday when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly on euro/yen, were in part aimed at providing better levels for these investors to hedge at and thus limit their book losses. \par \par \uc2  If so, the bank has had some success since the euro was up at 126.69/85 yen at the midsession from an early 125.35/45 and a lifetime low of 122.60 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  And by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  today at such high levels, dealers conceded the BOJ had managed to clear major chart resistance on the both the dollar and euro, offering at least the chance of a technical uptrend developing. \par \par \uc2  The dollar broke significant levels at 120.90, 121.20 and 122.00 yen and briefly cleared 122.45 before running into heavy offers. A close above the latter level would be very bullish and should herald a return to the year's highs around 124.80. \par \par \uc2  The euro, meanwhile, has taken a big retracement target at 126.60 yen and analysts now look for a push to 127.65, which was the rejection high from May 31. \par \par \uc2  ((Wayne Cole, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8584 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6l061jf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
