\par\par \b \uc2  Japan MOF Kuroda:  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Stability Disirable \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1999\par 21:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  COLOGNE (Dow Jones)--It is desirable that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates move in a stable manner, Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of the international bureau at the Japanese Finance Ministry said Friday. \par \par \uc2  Stability in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is desirable especially at a time when Japan's economy is at an important juncture, Kuroda said on the sidelines of the meeting of leaders from the Group of Seven leading industrialized nations. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the day to support the euro against the yen, he declined to comment directly. But he said that "it is a fact that there has been an action in the market." Kuroda said that the action "was taken in light of recent market conditions." \par \par \uc2  "We have taken appropriate measures in the past and will do so in the future," he said. \par \par \uc2  Kuroda's comments come hours after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed that it bought euros for yen on behalf of the Bank of Japan earlier in the day. "The ECB can confirm that the European System of Central Banks (ESCB) bought euros against yen on behalf of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the ECB said. \par \par \uc2  In reaction to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro surged more than two yen, and the dollar rose a yen as well. The euro rose to $1.0400, up from levels around $1.0300 at 1135 GMT, when the move began, and to Y125.05, above Y122.85 before the move. The dollar rose to Y120.25, above Y119.30 earlier. Late in New York trade, the euro was trading at Y125.11, and the dollar was at Y120.48. \par \par \uc2  -By Chikako Mogi; cmogi@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 18-06-99 \par \par \uc2  1923GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6i04lte\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
