\par\par \b \uc2  Schroeder not worried on euro - Japan official. \b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1999\par 15:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  COLOGNE, Germany, June 18 (Reuters) - German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder was quoted on Friday by a Japanese official as saying he was not worried about the strength of the euro. \par \par \uc2  A Japanese Foreign Ministry official quoted Schroeder telling Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi: "I am not concerned at all about the strength of the euro because all euro members support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Obuchi expressed his hope that the relationship between the euro and the yen would be "closer", the Japanese official said after the two leaders met ahead of the World Economic Summit in Cologne. The official did not elaborate. \par \par \uc2  The leaders' comments came after the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to buy euros and sell yen at the request of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in the past two weeks to contain the appreciation of the yen against the euro, which has depreciated steadily on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since its launch last January. \par \par \uc2  After the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the euro bounced to 125.06/18 from a lifetime low of 122.60 hit earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6i06958\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
