\par\par \b \uc2  ECB confirms bought euro vs yen for Bank of Japan. \b0\par\par\uc2 466 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1999\par 15:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT, Germany (Reuters) - The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets buying euros against yen upon the request of the Bank of Japan. \par \par \uc2  "We can confirm that on behalf of the Bank of Japan, we bought euros against yen," an ECB spokesman said. \par \par \uc2  A Bundesbank spokesman declined to comment on the ECB's confirmation. \par \par \uc2  The individual 11 central banks within the European System of Central Banks who are taking part in European Monetary Union are not allowed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  except by mutual agreement, the Bundesbank spokesman said. \par \par \uc2  A statement from the Bundesbank was possible later Friday, he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders in New York said Germany's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been selling the yen on the cross against the euro moments after the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had appreciated as far as 122.60 per euro, its best showing since the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's launch in January. \par \par \uc2  The U.S Treasury and Federal Reserve have declined to comment on whether U.S. monetary authorities took part in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in the past two weeks to curb yen gains. But on both occasions, traders said it had sold yen for dollars. \par \par \uc2  The euro spiked up sharply against the dollar and the yen on the news, trading at $1.0407 and 125.25 yen around midday. \par \par \uc2  The euro leaped as much as two yen and half a cent against the dollar earlier in the space of minutes as traders cited rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales. \par \par \uc2  A Bundesbank spokesman declined to comment on the ECB's confirmation. \par \par \uc2  The individual 11 central banks within the European System of Central Banks who are taking part in European Monetary Union are not allowed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  except by mutual agreement, the Bundesbank spokesman said. \par \par \uc2  A statement from the Bundesbank was possible later in the day, he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders in New York said Germany's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been selling the yen on the cross against the euro moments after the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had appreciated as far as 122.60 per euro, its best showing since the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's launch in January. \par \par \uc2  The U.S Treasury and U.S. Federal Reserve have declined to comment on whether U.S. monetary authorities took part in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in the past two weeks, once on July 10 and again on Monday, to curb yen gains. But on both occassions, traders said it had sold yen for dollars. \par \par \uc2  The euro spiked up sharply against the dollar and the yen on the news, trading at $1.0407 and 125.25 yen around 1236 GMT. ((Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525, frankfurt.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6i06942\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picsc