\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-Japan boosts its exchange rate armoury. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1999\par 21:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 18 (Reuters) - Japan's recruitment of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to its campaign to control the unruly yen demonstrates its ability to use central banking connections as a booster for its own exchange rate armoury. \par \par \uc2  Japan channelled sales of yen for euros through the ECB on Friday as the world's most powerful nations were meeting in Cologne, Germany and as bilateral talks between German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder and Japanese Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi took place. \par \par \uc2  Its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the third time it has sold yen in less than two weeks to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength. The move underlined Japan's commitment to ensuring its economic recovery remained on track even as the country was being urged to do its utmost for its economy. \par \par \uc2  It was also seen as a demonstration of co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  between Japan and the 11-nation euro zone with the Bundesbank, the Bank of France, and the Bank of Italy all reported to have acted as conduits for sales of yen. These are the central banks of the three countries which are in both the euro zone and the G7. \par \par \uc2  While the United States was notable by its absence, analysts said the choice of euro/yen as a vehicle for Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to have found favour with euro zone politicians who did not have to use their own reserves to engineer a rise in their flagging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "This reinforces the idea of international co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and suits at least two out of three of the major powers," said Nick Parsons, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Paribas Capital Markets. \par \par \uc2  "There are no losers in this game and champagne corks will be popping in Cologne and Frankfurt tonight." \par \par \uc2  Expectations were reinforced that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would go down well with G7 leaders after a White House official said U.S. President Bill Clinton told Japanese Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi to use all tools at his disposal to spur Japanese growth. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile Obuchi told German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder that he hoped the relationship between the euro and the yen would be closer. \par \par \uc2  "The general perception is that this shouldn't be taken lightly," said Yuji Tashiro, a dealer at Daiwa Europe Bank. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that the BOJ went through the ECB means this is in effect a coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  This view was reflected by the broad-based surge in the euro seen in the wake of Japan's vicarious yen spending spree, which was rumoured to have totalled as much as $3 billion. \par \par \uc2  The European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  leapt more than three yen from a life low of 122.60 and pulled away from all-time lows against the dollar by leaping 1.25 cents to peaks of $1.0422. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar rallied as far as 120.94 yen, its strongest in one and a half weeks and nearly two yen above the day's lows at 119.00. \par \par \uc2  The yen had returned to those levels despite the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own account twice last week and again on Monday during Asian trading hours, showing the limited effect of the bank's unassisted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But while traders said they were unlikely to test the Bank of Japan's resolve immediately, they were less convinced about the euro's ability to stay away from the life low of $1.0254 it plumbed on June 7. \par \par \uc2  "They are drawing a line under dollar/yen and euro/yen but I would not want to be long of euros given that that still looks like standing in front of a runaway train," said a senior trader at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6i061z6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
