\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-Yen sales have limited effect without Fed. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Svea Herbst-Bayliss \par \uc2 750 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1999\par 20:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, June 18 (Reuters) - Japan's yen sales on Friday are unlikely to make a lasting change in the yen's recent uptrend unless Washington plays along, something it is unlikely to do for at least the next few weeks, U.S. analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The United States would be understanably reluctant to tinker with the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by buying dollars now, just days before the Federal Reserve is expected to raise official interest rates and weeks before the Treasury Department is scheduled to get a new boss, they said. \par \par \uc2  "For the markets, the big question of course is what will the Fed do. If they should come in, it would be a huge signal from the G7. But if they don't there may be very little follow-through," Warburg Dillon Read analyst Tomas Jelf said. \par \par \uc2  After days of heavy-handed hints that Tokyo would strike back if the yen continued to shoot higher, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought euros for yen on the Bank of Japan's behalf several times during the morning. \par \par \uc2  Dealers saw the Bundesbank, the Bank of Italy, the Bank of France as well as the ECB itself selling yen while the Fed remained conspicuously absent. \par \par \uc2  "People were buzzing with talk of seeing Buba, Italy and so the spotlight was on the Fed but no one saw them," a dealer said. Washington declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Initially the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was effective, perhaps because selling on the euro/yen cross caught the market off guard. But by noon, euro/yen had given back nearly a full yen even though it remained comfortably above the 122.60 session low. \par \par \uc2  By extension, the dollar pared earlier gains against the yen to trade at 120.40/50 at 1300 EDT compared with the session's 120.94 high. The euro lost all of the ground it had gained against the dollar, slipping to $1.0377/84 from its $1.0422 high. \par \par \uc2  "For a short while people put on new long dollar/yen positions but now there just seems to be profit-taking with the trend for a firmer yen largely uninterrupted," a dealer at a U.S. investment bank said. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers predicted euro/yen may soon slip back into the 123 range as dollar/yen heads back toward the 119 handle it tested overnight in spite of Monday's large BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , estimated to have been around $10 billion. Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen to be smaller, near $3 billion. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan may have been particularly eager to hem in the yen now as leaders from the world's seven most industrialised nations and Russia meet in Cologne, Germany. \par \par \uc2  U.S. President Bill Clinton urged Japan's Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi to use all available tools to spur economic growth. Analysts said "all available tools" was shorthand for fiscal and monetary stimulus, and added Japan might have been embarrassed to face its partners as the yen surges. \par \par \uc2  But like last week and early this week, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not be enough to reverse a trend of new yen buying, sparked both by stronger growth figures and repatriation of funds. \par \par \uc2  "In the short run the market appears ready to test the Bank of Japan's resolve. Of course if the Fed were to come in, it would be different but I don't think they will," Chase \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Harvey Chen said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts agreed that U.S. participation in any yen-related \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - which would be the first since last summer - might unnerve financial markets at a critical time. \par \par \uc2  "It would complicate matters just before the Fed seems to be ready to raise rates and as Larry Summers is waiting to be confirmed as Treasury Secretary," Chen added. \par \par \uc2  Since financial markets reacted positively to hints from Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan that there may be only one preemptive tightening, dealers expect the dollar to get a slight lift anyway. \par \par \uc2  And any open market dollar buying might simply accelerate pre-programmed dollar gains, particularly against the euro where the dealers are calling for new euro lows. \par \par \uc2  "Any Fed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have such a knock-on effect that they are going to try and keep their hands out of it for as long as possible in order not to upset everything else," a dealer at an investment bank concluded. \par \par \uc2  ((-N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1639 )). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6i061x1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
