\par\par \b \uc2  Japan stocks steady, await US reaction to Fed. \b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1999\par 16:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 18 (Reuters) - Japanese stocks in London were steady on Friday, with dealers waited for a cue from U.S. markets. \par \par \uc2  "It's been quite quiet. There has been some business but nothing trendy, just individual orders," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  - using the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen for euros to strengthen the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - had not caused any significant effect. \par \par \uc2  "We haven't seen any consequent interest in the blue chip sector. It's done very well because of the bounce in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last few days anywyay," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  "Most of us are waiting to see what sort of action we're going to see in the (United) States," he added. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan hinted strongly that the Fed was likely to raise U.S. rates only modestly in the short-term to avoid harsher medicine later. \par \par \uc2  The Nikkei 50 showed a 0.1 percent gain by 1400 GMT. Sony  dropped 25 yen to 122265 by that time. ((London newsroom +44 171 542 5106, fax +44 171 542 2120, uk.equities.news@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6i060x9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
