\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Asia: BOJ Sterilization Shows Weaker Yen Not Favored \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 758 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1999\par 07:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sterilization of Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one more signal that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic situation, if not exactly improving, is at least getting no worse. \par \par \uc2  By clawing back from the money markets on Wednesday the yen that it sold in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  clearly indicated that while it doesn't want the yen to strengthen, neither is it prepared to countenance yen weakness. \par \par \uc2  Had the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  been really serious about its dollar-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, it would have left its yen sales unsterilized when the transactions settled two days later, as it did in January when it last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2  As it was, however, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issued Y1.1 trillion in commercial bills Wednesday morning to re-absorb the estimated $10 billion worth of yen it had sold two days previously. \par \par \uc2  "The decision by the BOJ to sterilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was key. It has sent a message to the market that there is no imminent change in monetary policy," explained analysts at State Street Bank in a research note dated Thursday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    BOJ Rejects Easier Monetary Stance\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Had the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chosen not to offset its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through the money market, observers would have taken its\par decision not to mop up the yen liquidity created by Monday's action as a\par crucial indicator of a more aggressive policy of monetary easing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For months now the Bank of Japan has been pursuing a policy of\par maintaining short-term interest rates at zero. But ultra-low borrowing\par costs haven't provided quite the monetary stimulus the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had\par expected, partly because, as the margins earned by participants in the\par money markets have evaporated, the BOJ has encountered unforeseen\par difficulties in injecting cash into the system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Thursday morning, for example, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  received only Y228\par billion of offers for the Y300 billion of discount bills it had planned\par to buy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With persistent deflationary pressure suppressing domestic demand,\par many economists have called upon the BOJ to adopt a more drastic program\par of active monetary expansion to reflate the economy. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par they argue, should switch to utilizing quantitative money-supply\par targeting, rather than interest-rate targeting, as its principal tool of\par monetary policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although a U-turn in favor of quantitative easing has been widely\par written off as too radical a policy change for the hidebound BOJ, some\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -watchers have suggested that unsterilized \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would provide the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with a back-door means by\par which it could successfully expand money supply.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There is always a bid and offer in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market,"\par explained Bank of America analysts in a research note issued on\par Wednesday. "Just as the swap market became a source of yen funding for\par Japanese banks when the Japan premium made it difficult for them to\par borrow, it is conceivable that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market could become\par an arena for BOJ \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to supply funds to the domestic market."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Yen Stability Crucial To Consumer Confidence\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By sterilizing Monday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has firmly\par rejected that option. To some market-watchers, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par decision indicates that there is no need for desperate measures to\par reflate the domestic economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The Bank of Japan is achieving pretty much everything it wants to\par achieve with its monetary policy at the moment," says Clifford Bennett,\par Sydney-based senior regional treasury strategist at Banque Nationale de\par Paris.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par According to Bennett, now that the Japanese economy is showing signs\par of picking up following GDP growth of 1.9% in the first quarter, the\par BOJ's primary objective is to foster a sense of confidence among\par domestic consumers. To do that, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  must emphasize\par stability above all else.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Now that they can see a glimmer of light at the end of the tunnel,\par the central bankers don't want to rock the boat. They certainly don't\par want to be seen to be panicking," says Bennett, arguing that\par exchange-rate instability would once again send Japanese consumers\par running for shelter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The very last thing the Bank of Japan wants to see is a drastic\par appreciation of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but equally it doesn't want to see the yen\par depreciate drastically."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-06-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0527GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4258 5095 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6h04k7r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
