\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr down on euro/yen sales,BOJ caution limits drop. \b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1999\par 03:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 17 (Reuters) - The dollar was slightly lower against the yen in early Tokyo on Thursday, dragged down by euro selling for yen. \par \par \uc2  But the U.S. unit was still supported after an overnight U.S. asset market rally and expectations of possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 120.17/27 yen at 0040 GMT, compared with 120.33/43 yen in New York late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "Japanese investors still need to sell more euro to hedge their portfolios. Exporters are also falling behind in meeting hedging needs for euro/yen," said a dealer at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 123.93/99 yen, compared with 124.06 yen in New York late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the euro could eventually test 123.18 yen, its lifetime low hit on June 10. \par \par \uc2  "If the euro/yen rate sets another record low, Japanese selling could intensify," said a dealer at a trust bank. \par \par \uc2  Japan's current account surplus fell 16.5 percent in April from a year earlier to 885.4 billion yen, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said earlier on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The market had expected a surplus of around one trillion yen, but the data failed to lift the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment, there isn't much interest in trade numbers. People are now most interested in (Federal Reserve Chairman Alan) Greenspan's testimony," said the city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan is scheduled to testify on monetary policy and the economic outlook before the Joint Economic Committee of Congress at 1400 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat Eisuke Sakakibara was silent on exchange rates on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Asked by reporters about the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Sakakibara, vice finance minister for international affairs, said: "I have no comment today." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar looked in better shape after U.S. stocks and bonds rallied overnight on subdued inflation data. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. May Consumer Price Index (CPI) was unchanged after a 0.7 percent jump in April. The core CPI, which excludes volatile food and energy prices, rose just 0.1 percent. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's upside was still capped against the yen by offers from Japanese exporters and investors, dealers said. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6h06cpo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
