\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CROSS - Euro capped by Japanese hedging interest. \b0\par\par\uc2 623 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 1999\par 05:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 16 (Reuters) - The euro was slightly higher against the yen in Tokyo midday on Wednesday due to short-covering, but it remained capped by hedging interest from Japanese institutional investors and exporters, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Activity was quiet as the market awaited the release of the U.S. May consumer price index (CPI) at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "The euro gained slightly as some dealers squared their short positions after recently confirming a solid support around 125 yen," said a dealer at a Japanese trust bank. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 125.74/84 yen at 0259 GMT, compared with 125.52 yen in New York late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The euro seems to be finding a solid floor, but a lot of investors here had invested too heavily in European bonds and are still looking to hedge their portfolio," said a dealer at a Japanese city bank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the downside of the euro is likely to be limited against the yen in the very near term, as the yen was capped by speculation that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen for dollars to prevent the dollar from falling below 120 yen. \par \par \uc2  "As long as the dollar's support at 120 yen holds, I don't think there will be any sharp euro/yen sell-off," said the city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday in Tokyo to buy dollars, pushing the greenback as high as 120.90 yen from a low of 117.87 yen on that day. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 120.50/60 yen, compared with 120.35/45 yen in New York late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But the market might test 120 yen and also push the euro/yen rate down if U.S. asset markets react negatively to the U.S. CPI data, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. economists polled by Reuters forecast, on average, a month-on-month CPI rise of 0.2 percent in May after April's 0.7 percent jump. The core CPI is also expected to rise 0.2 percent in May after a 0.4 percent rise in April. \par \par \uc2  The market also will be watching a news conference by BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami at 0600 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "Reactions in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will depend on how Japanese interest rates move on Hayami's comments," said a dealer at another trust bank. \par \par \uc2  Speculation that the BOJ might end its zero interest rate policy heighted late last week in the wake of a robust 7.9 percent annualised growth in Japan's January-March gross domestic product. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said that speculation has receded. \par \par \uc2  "Today's BOJ report showed that there was no big change in the BOJ's economic assessment," said the trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ said in its monthly report released earlier on Wednesday: "The economy has stopped deteriorating, but there are no clear movements towards recovery." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said latent downward pressure on prices remained. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at 192.18/30 yen, slightly up from 191.92 yen in late on Tuesday in New York, but still under pressure amid speculation that British interest rates could fall further. \par \par \uc2  That speculation was fuelled on Tuesday by a drop in Britain's May underlying inflation rate to a six-year low of 2.1 percent from April's 2.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market would be watching Britain's May labour market statistics due at 0830 GMT for more clues. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Swiss franc was at 78.76/81 yen, compared with 78.64 yen in New York late on Tuesday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-3432-9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6g06dsi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
