\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Dollar eyeballs 120 yen, euro soft. \b0\par\par\uc2 622 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 1999\par 10:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 16 (Reuters) - The dollar edged down to within a whisker of 120 yen on Wednesday after the Bank of Japan squelched talk of further monetary easing overnight by absorbing the surplus yen arising from its recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It looks like the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  did sterilise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which I think is a little bit disappointing to the market," said David Bloom, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HSBC Markets, referring to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight. \par \par \uc2  The euro slipped below $1.04 as momentum from last week's recovery rally waned, and sterling fell to three-week lows against the dollar on talk of more British interest rate cuts. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 120.15/25 yen at 0755 GMT after dipping to a low of 120.08 from 120.58/63 in Tuesday's late European session. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had earlier gained on speculation that the BOJ might not absorb excess yen liquidity resulting from its huge dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday. That would have meant lower yen interest rates, widening the interest differential between the dollar and yen. \par \par \uc2  But as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  drained a good part of the day's surplus in the banking system, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  softened, despite lingering fear of further BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar further closed in on the psychologically important 120.00-yen level as some short-term traders unwound their long dollar positions after BOJ governor Masaru Hayami repeated Japanese officials' recent assessment of the economy. \par \par \uc2  Hayami said the BOJ would maintain its easy monetary policy until deflation worries subsided and that the strong first quarter growth data last week did not mean the private sector could sustain recovery. He said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign exchanges was not a tool for monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  Overnight, ratings agency Standard & Poor's affirmed its AAA rating for Japan's long-term sovereign debt. \par \par \uc2  While \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not immediately react, traders said it was in line with the market's reduced pessimism about Japan. \par \par \uc2  The euro ratcheted down to the $1.0390 area after drifting overnight in a narrow range largely around $1.0420, near late Tuesday levels. \par \par \uc2  Traders said flows had thinned ahead of May U.S. consumer prices data due out at 1230 GMT. \par \par \uc2  In the absence of positive news on the European economy, the market focused on interest rate differentials, which could further widen in favour of the dollar should the Federal Reserve tighten credit at its upcoming policy-making meeting, they said. \par \par \uc2  "It looks like the euro's rally last week proved to be short-lived," said a Japanese bank trader in London. "It's pretty quiet at the moment, although we'll probably see lower levels eventually." \par \par \uc2  A U.S. bank trader said $1.0380 was a key support. \par \par \uc2  "It won't take very much for the euro to continue its downward slide if that level breaks," he said. \par \par \uc2  The market showed little reaction to a 0.3 percent rise on the month in Germany's May wholesale prices - a 2.5 percent decline from a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  The pound fell to three-week lows below $1.59 after Tuesday's weak inflation data fuelled speculation of further Bank of England credit easing to follow last week's 25 basis point rate cut. \par \par \uc2  Sterling made a slight recovery after news May UK claimant count unemployment fell 6,500 against an average forecast for a rise of 2,500. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.5900/05 shortly after the data, compared with a session low of $1.5882 and $1.5946/56 late in Europe on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Shin Kishima, London Capital Markets +44-171-542-4407)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6g06a7k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
