\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Euro struggles near one-week lows. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,057 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1999\par 13:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 15 (Reuters) - The euro struggled near one-week lows below $1.04 in European trading on Tuesday as last week's recovery rally lost steam amid a dearth of positive news on the European economy. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was pressured against the yen amid talk of heavy selling interest at higher levels, but fear of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  held the greenback above 120. \par \par \uc2  "It's beginning to show slightly alarming signs of renewed weakness," Dick Howard, director of economic research at Julius Baer Investments in London, said of the euro's dip below $1.04. \par \par \uc2  Traders said repeated failure last week to sustain gains above $1.05 prompted short-term traders to give up on their long euro positions for now. \par \par \uc2  Howard said the European economy was probably picking up but only slowly. \par \par \uc2  A 1.4-percent month-on-month fall in April Italian industrial output gave euro bears a reason to probe the downside, he added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar popped up a quarter yen at mid-session on buying from large U.S. investment banks amid a market still nervous about BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  London bank dealers were sceptical if the buy orders came from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , noting bank names that were on the bid side in electronic trading systems. \par \par \uc2  Still, they said the move reflected the market's jumpiness after Monday's huge \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said to have totaled between five and 10 billion dollars. \par \par \uc2  Besides the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  factor, the general bias was still to the downside, they added. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment, it looks like the yen is trying to head back in the direction that the BOJ was preventing it from going," Howard said. "It suggests that a fair amount of impetus for a stronger yen in the near future." \par \par \uc2  Junpei Yamamoto, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank of Tokyo, said there appeared to be a lot of long dollar positions in expectation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He predicted that those short-term traders were likely to take profit in the upper-120 yen area and cut losses below 119.70 or so. \par \par \uc2  "We'll have to see these positions cleaned out before we can see a big move in either direction," he said. \par \par \uc2  "So the evidence will be slow to come through," he said. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably just hover around these levels for a while before the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is convinced that the European economy is in a healthier shape." \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 120.54/59 yen at 1140 GMT after trading most of the day in the 120.20/30 area, roughly where it had been late in Monday's European session. \par \par \uc2  Japanese investors' appetite for dollar assets was curbed at the moment by concerns of a U.S. credit tightening. The market is awaiting Wednesday's May U.S. consumer price index and Thursday's testimony by Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan before the Joint Economic Committee, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Sterling softened a little as the British retail price index came in below expectations, undershooting government's 2.5 percent inflation target. \par \par \uc2  May RPI was up 0.2 percent month-on-month against a 0.4 percent rise forecast. It was up 1.3 percent year-on-year against expectations of a 1.4 percent rise. \par \par \uc2  The pound stood at $1.5999/04 against $1.6087/92 late on Monday. Euro/sterling stood at 6502/04 pence versus 64.76/78. \par \par \uc2  UK Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown told a parliamentary committee that Britain had no intention of rejoining the exchange rate mechanism \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  grid and any decision to join the euro would be based on national interests. \par \par \uc2  A 1.4-percent month-on-month fall in April Italian industrial output gave euro bears a reason to probe the downside, he added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar popped up a quarter yen at mid-session on buying from large U.S. investment banks amid a market still nervous about BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  London bank dealers were sceptical if the buy orders came from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , noting bank names that were on the bid side in electronic trading systems. \par \par \uc2  Still, they said the move reflected the market's jumpiness after Monday's huge \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said to have totaled between five and 10 billion dollars. \par \par \uc2  Besides the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  factor, the general bias was still to the downside, they added. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment, it looks like the yen is trying to head back in the direction that the BOJ was preventing it from going," Howard said. "It suggests that a fair amount of impetus for a stronger yen in the near future." \par \par \uc2  Junpei Yamamoto, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank of Tokyo, said there appeared to be a lot of long dollar positions in expectation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He predicted that those short-term traders were likely to take profit in the upper-120 yen area and cut losses below 119.70 or so. \par \par \uc2  "We'll have to see these positions cleaned out before we can see a big move in either direction," he said. \par 