\par\par \b \uc2  JGBs higher on weak data, steady cash buying. \b0\par\par\uc2 860 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1999\par 10:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 15 (Reuters) - Japanese government bond (JGB) prices were higher in late Tokyo trade on Tuesday, as weak economic data prompted the market to rethink the economy's prospects and last week's strong first-quarter growth figures. \par \par \uc2  The market also cheered the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (MOF) decision to maintain the July issuance of 10-year JGBs at a reduced level of 1.4 trillion yen in order stem a rise in long-term interest rates. \par \par \uc2  September JGBs closed at the session high of 132.65, up 0.80 from Monday. The yield on the key 213th 10-year bond was at 1.595 percent, down from Monday's close of 1.635 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealer-led buybacks also helped to boost the contract after it found firm support near the intraday low of 132.07. \par \par \uc2  "Following the strong GDP data (released last Thursday), the market's focus has switched to the economy," said a trader at a city bank. \par \par \uc2  The Trade Ministry said on Tuesday afternoon that Japan's April industrial production was revised downward to a decline of 3.4 percent month-on-month, compared with a preliminary figure of a 2.7 percent drop. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo department store sales for May fell 2.5 percent from a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  The yield curve flattened further, amid steady buying interest at the long end. \par \par \uc2  Some public financial institutions were continuing to buy into the 10-year sector, traders said, with strong interest in the 212th bond. \par \par \uc2  Some life insurers were also seen switching from the 10-year and 20-year sector to the medium-term zone, especially the 6-year sector, traders said. \par \par \uc2  But dealers were wary of chasing prices higher after the yield on the key 213th bond fell to 1.600 percent. \par \par \uc2  "We saw bull-flattening trades on Monday, and it continued to flatten today, but I don't know how long this trend will continue now that the 213th bond has hit 1.6 percent," said a dealer at a bank-affiliated brokerage. \par \par \uc2  A senior MOF official, briefing reporters on the July bond issuance volume, said that the ministry will watch market movements to determine the issuance of 10-year JGBs in and after August. \par \par \uc2  MOF also said on Tuesday that it will continue buying JGBs outright from the market for the time being in and after July. \par \par \uc2  The ministry will also raise its planned monthly offering of one-year Treasury bills (TB) and two-year and six-year JGBs in July, to help offset a reduction in its planned 10-year JGB issuance. \par \par \uc2  But that would result in a net rise of 300 billion yen in monthly bond issuance in July compared with the April-June period unless the volume of other maturities is reduced. \par \par \uc2  A senior MOF official, speaking to Reuters, declined to comment on the matter and said that, for maturities not included in Tuesday's announcement, the ministry would announce the offering volume one week prior to their next auction. \par \par \uc2  "I think we can applaud the government's determination to keep bond yields in check...and prevent the yen from appreciating. Their stance indicates they are not confident about the economy yet," a trader at another city bank said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) was seen actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Monday and also on June 10, pushing the dollar up by about three yen to more than 120 yen. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the key March TIBOR-based euroyen futures contract was at 99.74, up from Monday's day session close of 99.65. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ left the money market in surplus by 1.2 trillion yen after its regular 0020 GMT \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , up from 1.0 trillion yen after the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday. \par \par \uc2  A BOJ official said on Tuesday there was no change in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance in the money market, despite the higher fund surplus. \par \par \uc2  "We also left a surplus of 1.2 trillion yen on the final day (of the bank resrve period) last month, so this does not mean that the Bank of Japan has changed its stance (in the money market)," the official said. \par \par \uc2  The overnight call rate traded mainly at 0.03 percent, unchanged from the most-heavily traded rate on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers will closely watch the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, when \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade settlements occur, to see whether the yen added to the money market is sterilised through money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The BOJ on Monday was said to have bought more than $5 billion and perhaps as much as $10 billion for yen, which would have resulted in the injection of some one trillion yen into the banking system. \par \par \uc2  If the BOJ refrains from draining the additional funds and leaves a large surplus in the money market, that would be a sign of quantitative easing, some analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "Since the size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was apparently large, we want to check the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday," the bank-affiliated brokerage dealer said. ((Tamawa Kadoya, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6f06g10\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\