\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ seen 'sterilising' huge  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tamawa Kadoya \par \uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 1999\par 13:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 15 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will effectively wipe out the impact of, or "sterilise", its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market, sticking to its current easy monetary policy, money market traders say. \par \par \uc2  Traders played down market speculation that the BOJ would adopt a reflationary policy by leaving Monday's dollar-buying, yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "unsterilised" - in this case, refraining from absorbing the additional yen funds it created. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ is not convinced that adding more liquidity to the money market would work to boost the economy when the system is already caught in a liquidity trap," a source close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  Shigeyasu Kobayashi, chief manager of the treasury and investment division at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi, said: "The BOJ's Policy Board did not announce any new policy directives. So there is no point in the BOJ keeping more than its current net surplus by increasing the surplus by another trillion yen in the money market to conduct its present monetary policy." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said after its board met on Monday that it decided to maintain its current easy monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ has left a net surplus of one trillion yen or more in the money market since February 26 to conduct its policy of setting its key policy indicator, the overnight call rate, effectively at zero. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ has indicated through its daily money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it can conduct its policy directive of setting interest rates at zero by keeping a surplus of one trillion yen," Kobayashi said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ on Monday repeatedly stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy over $5 billion for yen, pushing the greenback as high as 120.90 yen from an earlier low of 117.87. \par \par \uc2  That would represent an injection of yen funds of over some 600 billion yen or more resulting from the action. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said the BOJ had already taken steps to absorb the excess funds created by Monday's dollar-buying action. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ announced on Tuesday it would offer to sell 1.1 trillion yen worth of discount bills via an auction on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to absorb the yen funds from the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although it's difficult to say this amount is the the actual size of the BOJ's action," a senior dealer at another major city bank said. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ could have attempted to drain the funds at its regular morning \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  (on Wednesday). But there may have been a risk of not being able to attract enough bids to do so," he said. \par \par \uc2  According to the BOJ's fund supply/demand projections, it expects a net surplus of 2.33 trillion yen in the money market on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Money market participants think the BOJ will drain 1.2 or 1.3 trillion yen from the market to leave a net surplus of around 1.0 trillion yen after its regular 0020 GMT \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 .... \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6f064nf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal