\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Tanami -2: After BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  Repeatedly Mon \b0\par\par\uc2 151 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 10:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--A sudden strengthening of the yen is undesirable for the Japanese and global economies, the top bureaucrat at the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeated Monday. \par \par \uc2  At a regular news conference, Administrative Vice Minister Koji Tanami said: "As I said before, a sudden strengthening in the yen is not good, not only for the Japanese economy, but for the global economy as well." \par \par \uc2  He continued: "(\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) action was taken today in the market based on this judgment. As \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability is vital, we will continue to carefully monitor movements (in the dollar-yen), taking appropriate action as needed." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen Monday, sending the dollar about three yen higher from the intraday low of Y117.91 to a high of Y120.83 during Asian trade. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 14-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0837GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6e04iy0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
