\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Aggressive BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Pushes Dlr Up \b0\par\par\uc2  By James Simms \par \uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 08:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Aggressive, repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  brought the dollar up almost three yen Monday in Asia despite strong selling interest from U.S. funds. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the morning just as Japanese monetary officials issued strong verbal warnings against yen strength, and the dollar quickly shot up above Y119 from an intraday low of Y117.91. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the BOJ then continued to come into the market, selling yen at Y118.20, Y118.80, Y119.20, Y119.50 and Y120.00 in an attempt to buoy the dollar above Y120. Some said Japanese authorities may want to push the dollar as high as Y122.00 in the Tokyo session. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pretty pesky," said Hirokazu Note, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Sumitomo Bank. "There's really no one else that would be buying now." \par \par \uc2  "They've been in continually, at least five or six times," said a European bank trader in the late morning, adding that the market would be watching for more BOJ action in London. \par \par \uc2  Still, the persistance of the BOJ is virtually the only factor giving the dollar an upside, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "With just the authorities buying, without any private follow-through, it'll be hard to hit Y122, or Y125," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at a Japanese bank. "U.S. funds liquidating long dollar positions are taking advantage of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The U.S. funds are said to be selling into the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to repatriate yen carry trade positions. \par \par \uc2  At 0530 GMT (1:15 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y120.60, above Y117.95 late Friday in New York and up from Y117.97 late Friday in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0490, lower than $1.0528 late Friday in New York but below $1.0499 in London Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0607GMT \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6e04iad\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
