\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Asia: Both Bulls And Bears Heartened By BoJ Action \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tom Holland \par \uc2 815 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 07:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG (Dow Jones)--Yen bears argue that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday proves their point. \par \par \uc2  So do yen bulls. \par \par \uc2  According to the bears, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is acting to damp market reaction to Japan's unexpectedly high first-quarter GDP figures, released last week. Aware that the 1.9% growth recorded in the first quarter was a one-off aberration produced by fiscal expansion, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to prevent the exchange rate deviating too far from levels consistent with poor underlying fundamentals, say the bears. \par \par \uc2  On the contrary, insist the bulls, by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar, the Japanese authorities are demonstrating that yen strength is a real issue that is being taken seriously in Tokyo. The authorities' action, they say, is clear evidence that the strong dollar/weak yen trend has finally reversed direction, and that the yen is now set on an upward path against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Whichever view turns out to be correct over the long term, there was no disputing the market's direction on Monday. A sustained barrage of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  - both verbal and physical - lifted the U.S. dollar by nearly three yen against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday morning. \par \par \uc2  While the Bank of Japan repeatedly bought U.S. dollars at levels from Y118 all the way up to Y120 and above, a clutch of heavy hitters from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed in to talk down the yen, warning the market not to underestimate the authorities' determination to prevent excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Hedge Funds Exit Short Yen Trades\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the short term, said dealers, the dollar has come under pressure\par from hedge fund sales. Facing heavy redemptions and hit hard by the\par recent sell-off in the U.S. Treasury market, a number of funds have sold\par dollars in order to exit the short yen positions with which they had\par funded their long Treasury trades.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar has also seen selling from conventional money managers\par looking to raise their weightings to Japanese equities following the\par release of the first-quarter GDP data last week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If that's all that was behind the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's fall against the\par yen, then the Bank of Japan's attempt to support the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is\par likely to be successful.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The extent of hedge fund liquidations is finite. And after buying $39\par billion worth of Japanese shares in the last 12 months, foreign\par institutions are now close to a neutral weighting to Japanese equities,\par limiting further likely inflows, according to U.S. custodian bank State\par Street.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against these flows, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can easily succeed in maintaining\par the dollar/yen exchange rate in the Bank of Japan's comfort zone of Y120\par to Y125. And as an added bonus, it will help achieve the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par monetary policy objectives by injecting liquidity into the yen money\par markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Some See Sustainable Upturn In Japan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But not all observers accept that view.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some are less ready to dismiss Japan's first-quarter growth numbers as\par an anomaly. They point to the rise in Asian regional exports to Japan\par over recent months as evidence that Japanese economic growth is likely\par to be sustained into the second quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par According to figures compiled by Nomura International, Singapore's\par exports to Japan were up by 18.4% year-on-year in April, compared with\par an 18.3% year-on-year fall in 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Over the same period, Malaysia's exports to Japan rose by 48%, in\par contrast to a 19.5% fall in 1998, while May saw Taiwanese exports to\par Japan increase by 30.4%, reversing a 20.2% decline in 1998.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Nomura's data also show a turnaround in exports to Japan from China,\par South Korea and Indonesia, while declines in exports from Hong Kong and\par Thailand slowed sharply, demonstrating a clear upturn in Japanese\par economic activity.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With Japan showing signs of recovery, and U.S. asset markets looking\par top-heavy ahead of an impending interest-rate hike, the outflows of\par Japanese capital which have long supported the dollar against the yen\par may be set to slow, or even reverse, warn the yen bulls.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par If they are right, there will be little the Bank of Japan can do to\par prevent the yen strengthening over the longer term. Faced with the\par combined forces of trade and capital flows, the most the authorities\par will be able to do is to step into the market on an occasional basis to\par moderate excessively volatile upward moves in the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par According to some market watchers, that, rather than a reversal of the\par short-term trend, was the purpose of Monday's action.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Tom Holland; 852 2832 2341; tom.holland@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-06-99\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0558GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  4258 5095 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6e04i95\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
