\par\par \b \uc2  Japan/Tanami/Miyazawa -2: Asked If More BOJ Moves Likely \b0\par\par\uc2 160 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 05:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TOKYO (Nikkei/Dow Jones)--The top bureaucrat at Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Monday that an excessively strong yen isn't good for a\par recovery in the country's economy.\par    Asked if the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par markets, Administrative Vice Finance Minister Koji Tanami said, "An\par excessively strong yen is undesirable for an economic recovery."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa also said Monday that disruptive\par movements in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets are not good.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  Earlier Monday, vice finance minister for international affairs, Eisuke Sakakibara confirmed that the BOJ had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stem the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  Around 0315 GMT (11:15 p.m. EDT Sunday), the dollar was trading at Y120.40, more than two yen above its intraday low of Y117.91. The dollar was at Y117.95 in New York late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0326GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6e04hyw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
