\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  CROSS-BOJ yen sales lift euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 08:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 14 (Reuters) - The euro strengthened sharply against the yen by Tokyo afternoon on Monday as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  put heavy pressure on the Japanese unit across the board, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the euro faced strong sales on rallies above 126 yen from sales led by Japanese life insurance firms, U.S. fund operators and exporters, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Euro/yen jumped in line with strength in dollar/yen, but the euro's gains were somewhat limited," a European bank dealer said. "Japanese insurers were eagerly waiting to sell the euro on rallies." \par \par \uc2  At 0544 GMT, the euro stood at 126.43/59 yen against 124.19 yen in late New York on Friday. The European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  briefly fell below 124 yen in early trade. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the movement in dollar/yen was the main factor behind the rise in euro/yen. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively, selling the yen for dollars repeatedly from around 118.20 yen to above 120 yen, bankers said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was detected around 120.20-120.30 yen in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Eisuke Sakakibara said on Monday that the ministry would prevent any premature strengthening of the yen to help ensure the Japanese economy recovers. \par \par \uc2  "The market should not underestimate our firm intentions," Sakakibara, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara later confirmed the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister Koji Tanami and senior official Haruhiko Kuroda echoed the line that an excessive yen rise was unfavourable for Japan. \par \par \uc2  "The euro is expected to find support should the BOJ continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the yen. The euro was also expected to be supported with the Kosovo crisis out of the way," a Japanese commercial bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "But euro/yen still lacks the energy to rise convincingly as many Japanese operators are looking for chances to unload their long positions," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, sterling was quoted at 194.07/19 yen from around 190.69 yen in late New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Swiss franc was at 79.22/27 yen versus from around 77.73 yen in late New York on Friday. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk 81-3-5473-3748, tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6e06kwy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
