\par\par \b \uc2  JGBs rise on recovery doubts, but gains limited. \b0\par\par\uc2 439 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 05:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 14 (Reuters) - Japanese government bond (JGB) cash and futures prices were firmer by Tokyo midday on Monday, but traders were cautious about chasing them higher on rallies. \par \par \uc2  Underlying sentiment was fragile as many operators remained reluctant to build up their positions after Japanese first-quarter gross domestic product figures, released last Thursday, came in much stronger than expected. \par \par \uc2  But prices were well supported on dips following official comments suggesting that any economic recovery was still fragile and by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Eisuke Sakakibara said on Monday that the ministry would prevent any premature strengthening of the yen to help ensure that the Japanese economy recovers. \par \par \uc2  "The market should not underestimate our firm intentions," Sakakibara, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Sakakibara later confirmed that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively, selling the yen for dollars repeatedly from around 118.20 yen to above 120 yen, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  A trader at a Japanese trust bank said: "Sentiment in the JGB market has been depressed severely after the GDP data, but Japanese officials still believe talk of an economic recovery is premature and that is drawing bids on price dips." \par \par \uc2  The key September 10-year JGB futures contract was quoted at 131.47 by midday, up 0.60 from Friday's Tokyo close. \par \par \uc2  The yield of the 213th 10-year JGB fell 0.085 to 1.665 percent. \par \par \uc2  Traders said sentiment was lifted after institutional investors and public funds were detected buying long-dated maturities, with public funds rumoured to be buying 20-year "super-long" bonds. \par \par \uc2  But city banks were rumoured to have sold their short-and medium-term issues in early trade. \par \par \uc2  Traders said rumours that a U.S. hedge fund needs to close massive short positions in JGBs, a factor behind a rise in JGB prices in London on Friday, continued to provide a firm footing for the futures market. \par \par \uc2  Trade was expected to be nervous in the afternoon ahead of the BOJ's monetary policy meeting, but most participants were not anticipating a change in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ left the money market with a fund surplus of 1.0 trillion yen at 0020 GMT, unchanged from last Friday. \par \par \uc2  The key unsecured overnight call money was traded at 0.03 percent, steady from Friday's weighted average. ((Chikafumi Hodo, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 5473-3748 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6e06kmn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
