\par\par \b \uc2  MOF's Sakakibara confirms BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 186 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 03:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 14 (Reuters) - Senior Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official Eisuke Sakakibara confirmed that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, but he declined to comment at what levels the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether he would confirm apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ, Sakakibara, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters: "Yes." \par \par \uc2  "We have taken appropriate steps (today)," Sakakibara added. \par \par \uc2  "As I have said, in order to ensure the Japanese economy recovers, we will prevent excessive strength in the yen. We will continue to monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves and take decisive action if necessary," Sakakibara said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was detected buying dollars at 118.20 yen and again at 118.80 yen in early Tokyo trade, with some dealers saying the bank may have started buying from 117.90 yen. Later in mid-morning trade, the BOJ was seen repeatedly buying dollars for yen from around 119.30 yen, bankers said. ((Yoko Nishikawa, Tokyo Newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6e06gsz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
