\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia in a rut with yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,058 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 13:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 14 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased on Monday in tandem with the softer yen, but analysts said they would remain stuck in a benign rut until the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  made a bigger shift up or down. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah bucked the trend, lifted once more by post-election optimism. \par \par \uc2  Emerging European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were quiet, with the Hungarian forint slipping off the top of its 4.5 percent-wide trading band in stilted trade and the Polish zloty drifting ahead of expected privatisation inflows. \par \par \uc2  The Czech crown barely flickered at retail sales data seen by analysts as broadly positive, although it remained on an upward course against the euro. \par \par \uc2  Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were slightly down on late Friday levels as the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly to sap the yen's upward push against the dollar, fearing excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength could harm its economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen dipped below 118 in Asian trading but surged to a peak of 120.85 on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It eased back slightly in the London morning, but fresh yen gains were limited by fears the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have left orders to sell yen beyond its own time zone. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said players were still looking for pointers on the possibility of a U.S. interest rate hike when the Federal Reserve's policy making body meets at the end of this month. \par \par \uc2  Eyes will be on Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan, who is due to speak at 1400 GMT on Monday on the impact of high technology on jobs, wages and living standards, and on U.S. May consumer price and industrial production data published on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would stay range-bound, trading mainly on their own merits, until dollar/yen made a clear break through 118-117.50 or 122-123. \par \par \uc2  "With the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up dollar/yen, regional curencies look unable to make headway against the greenback near term despite the threat of a U.S. rate hike," analysts at Standard Chartered said in a note to clients. \par \par \uc2  This would not necessarily be unwelcome, analysts added, as stability against the dollar would help keep inflation in check and ease fears of dented export competitiveness in countries such as South Korea, Thailand and the Philippines. \par \par \uc2  But some suggested the Bank of Korea, which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three days running last week to cap the won's rise, might still be uncomfortable with current levels despite Monday's weaker turn. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Korea hasn't been shy about showing its hand, and that's going to continue," one \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst said. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think they really like it here between 1,180 and 1,160 (to the dollar). If dollar/yen stays in the 118-120 range I'm pretty sure the Korean authorities would rather have the won between 1,180 and 1,220." \par \par \uc2  The rupiah continued its upward push in volatile trade, breaking through 7,500 to the dollar bid for the first time this year, as political horsetrading got under way to form a new coalition government after last Monday's general election. \par \par \uc2  "The rupiah is in its own little world," said Gerry Celaya, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  technical analyst at American Express Bank in London, adding that a squeeze on outstanding long dollar positions could lift the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  further towards 7,300. \par \par \uc2  Counting remained very slow, with only one-third of the results in. The opposition Indonesian Democratic Party-Struggle (PDI-P) was well ahead with just under 38 percent of the vote, with the ruling Golkar party trailing in third place. \par \par \uc2  In Europe, commercial dollar orders knocked the forint down to around 2.22 percent above its basket parity from last week's steady 2.25 percent, the ceiling of its trading band. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a 50-basis-point cut in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight repo rate, and a 25-basis-point cut in the two-week deposit facility, had no immediate effect on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The zloty firmed slightly to be quoted at 3.57 percent above parity around 1015 GMT, from Friday's 3.41/3.31 percent, but the market was still waiting for imminent privatisation inflows to lift the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  towards its next resistance at four percent above the mid-point. ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates, including the change versus late New York trade the previous day and the change in the year to date.. ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , formerly quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to reflect new market norms. All other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are quoted against the dollar. ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the rise or fall of the dollar or euro value. ** Annual 