\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Wariness of BOJ bolsters dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 17:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 14 (Reuters) - The dollar held above 120 yen in Europe on Monday amid concern that the Bank of Japan could step in again to sell yen as it did overnight. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's second appearance on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in five days triggered a three-yen rally from the dollar's Asian lows, with speculation rife that it spent more than $5 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen gains. \par \par \uc2  "The market is reluctant to sell dollar/yen too aggressively given the Bank of Japan has made it clear that they don't want a stronger yen," said a senior trader at a European bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "They (the BOJ) actually mean business this time so I cannot see a lot of mileage on the downside for dollar yen." \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose as far as 120.85 yen on the back of Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but had eased to 120.34/38 yen by 1500 GMT. That was still above Asian lows just under 118. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the main aim of BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was to avoid premature yen gains from derailing \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's nascent recovery. \par \par \uc2  "Japanese officials are trying to eliminate \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations, which in practical terms involves keeping the yen as close to 120 (per dollar) as they possibly can," said Kevin Grice, senior economist at the American Express Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  But he added that optimism fuelled by the surprisingly strong Japanese GDP figures released last week and the recent buoyancy of the asset market would revive demand for the yen and risk triggering yet more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The yen might force the Japanese authority to step in again if it gets back towards 118 yen," Grice said. \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen probed the 118 area in the U.S. on Friday and overnight in what traders said was a test of the BOJ's resolve. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Ministry official Eisuke Sakakibara confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would take "decisive action if necessary" to prevent an excessive yen rise. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the euro drifted lower, shedding more than a cent from Friday's two-and-a-half week peak of $1.0558. Traders said the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ignored a report which showed the euro zone's gross domestic product rose by a stronger-than-expected 0.4 percent in the first quarter of 1999 from the prior quarter and was up 1.8 percent from a year ago. \par \par \uc2  However, they noted a shift towards anti-euro rightist parties in the European Parliament elections. \par \par \uc2  "The elections did not show much confidence in the euro," said a trader at a British bank. \par \par \uc2  Some of the dollar gains against the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were spurred by a rally of the U.S. unit against the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  Strong interest to buy dollars emerged after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  breached a chart barrier at 1.5260 francs and as it later sped to six-day peaks above 1.53 francs. \par \par \uc2  Gains in U.S. stocks added to the the overall firm tone of the dollar. The Dow Jones Industrial Average was up about 0.80 percent at 10,576.94 at 1534 GMT. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar ignored testimony by Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greespan on Monday, in which he made no reference to U.S. monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was stable, showing little reaction to either weaker-than-expected May UK producer prices data or European parliament election results, which showed Britain's Conservative party gaining seats after campaigning on a eurosceptic platform. \par \par \uc2  The pound made only modest gains against the euro, failing to capitalise on euro/dollar weakness as the market spotlight remained on dollar/yen following the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((Lisa Jucca, London Capital Markets +44-171-542-6721, elisabetta.jucca@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6e06ery\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
