\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Caution over rates prevails in Asian markets. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Regan Morris \par \uc2 563 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 12:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, June 14 (Reuters) - Caution prevailed in Asian markets on Monday as Tokyo stocks snapped a six-day winning streak to end 0.1 percent down and South Korean shares fell over three percent. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong stocks capped a volatile day with a gain of just 0.1 percent on futures-driven buying. \par \par \uc2  Markets were wary over whether the Federal Reserve would raise borrowing costs ahead of a June 29-30 meeting of monetary policy-makers. The Dow Jones industrial closed Friday down 1.2 percent at 10,490.51. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan's benchmark Nikkei 225\tab    average closed barely lower at 17,188.82, unable to sustain an earlier rise past the 17,300 barrier as profit-taking set in, traders said.\par The Hang Seng Index\tab   edged up to 13,007.57 as some players bet that HSBC's  share reorganisation would push the counter up, pulling the underlying index along with it.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Jason Tang, institutional sales trader at South China securities, said some investors were trying to push the index up before the expiry of the June futures contract.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korea Composite Stock Price Index\tab    closed down 3.2 percent at 821.91. "Worries over the possible hike of U.S. interest rates really hit the local market," said Koh Kyong-bae, a broker at Hyundai Securities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen's fall against the dollar also hurt Seoul shares. The dollar jumped over two percent against the yen after the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent a strong yen from ruining the chances of economic recovery. It was traded at 120.33/43 at 0935 GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was rumoured to have spent over $5 billion buying dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Australian stock market was closed on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore shares ended lower in a rare half-day delay in trading due to a technical glitch. The Straits Times Index (STI)\tab   closed 0.4 percent down to 2,058.38. Taiwan stocks pushed above 8,000 points but the TAIEX\tab    closed down 0.1 percent at 7,973.58. The New Zealand market finished down 4.3 percent at 2,115.86 in its quietest trading day in over two years, with brokers blaming the Australian long weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thai shares closed up 1.5 percent to 514.67, off the day's highs, on profit-taking.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The main Philippine index shares ended up one percent at 2,391.20. Malaysia's Composite Index\tab    was 1.3 percent higher by the close at 782.98.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesian stocks closed 1.7 percent up to 679.4 on the back of a stronger rupiah as confidence grew after last week's peaceful election.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Stocks in China closed up as the market took supportive comments by a top market regulator as official blessing for recent gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Shenzhen's hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  B index soared 9.9 percent to 113.35 after Chen Yaoxian, vice chairman of the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC), said the surge marked a recovery in an orderly market. Shanghai's hard \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  B shares closed up 6.8 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The key Bombay share index closed 0.5 percent down at 3,950.44, while Karachi's benchmark index was down 3.9 percent at 1,080.22 by 1014 GMT after talks between India and Pakistan to lower tensions over Kashmir failed.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6e06e3f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
