\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Options: Yen Volatilities Up Even After BOJ Move \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 05:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Volatilities implied by Japanese yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  options are slightly higher in Tokyo Monday compared to levels in New York Friday even after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar against the yen at various levels throughout the morning. \par \par \uc2  "When the dollar fell through Y118, volatilities went up to 13.3%. But even after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which relieved upward pressure on the yen, options were sold a bit," said a European bank trader. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , along with an avalanche of comments from Japanese government officials warning that yen strength before the economy had recovered was undesirable, was making traders wary of selling dollars for yen. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the BOJ had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, Eisuke Sakakibara, the vice finance minister for international affairs, replied in the affirmative saying, "Yes. We took appropriate steps." \par \par \uc2  "We are watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market situation closely. If needed, we will take decisive measures," he added. \par \par \uc2  Traders said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Y118.20, Y118.80, Y119.20, 119.50 and Y120.00 and appears to be continuing to try to push the dollar up, possibly as high as Y122.00, in the Tokyo session. \par \par \uc2  In the over-the-counter market, one-month at-the-money dollar/yen options imply volatility of 13.1% bid, up from 12.9% in New York Friday, and above 12.8% in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, they are unchanged at 9.6% from levels in New York Friday. Euro/dollar options were quoted at 9.8% in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  At 0325 GMT (11.25 p.m. EDT Sunday), the dollar is at Y120.40, up from Y117.95 late Friday in New York. The euro is at $1.0481, down from $1.0528 Friday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Risk-reversals favor dollar put options against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. Risk-reversals measure the market preference for either put or call options by the premium or discount applied. \par \par \uc2  -By James Simms, 813-5255-2940; jsimms@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 14-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0353GMT \par \par \uc2  1077 4127 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6e04i0q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
