\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr steady in early Asia, G7 offers no direction. \b0\par\par\uc2 611 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 1999\par 01:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 14 (Reuters) - The dollar moved narrowly near 118 yen in early Asia trade on Monday, as the market was uninspired by a weekend meeting of finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors of the Group of Seven (G7) industrial powers. \par \par \uc2  The greenback looked vulnerable against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said, amid recent bright signs in the Japanese economy and worries over U.S. asset markets. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar was expected to draw support from speculation on possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ). \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 118.02/07 yen at 2251 GMT, compared with 117.88/98 yen in New York late on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Several G7 finance ministers said on Saturday that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were not discussed at all at their one-day meeting in Frankfurt. \par \par \uc2  Responding to reporters' questions about the euro, Italian Treasury Minister Giuliano Amato said on Saturday: "No, we didn't speak about the euro." \par \par \uc2  Japan's Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said any rapid movements in the yen were unfavourable. \par \par \uc2  "Since last week, the yen has been moving rather rapidly. I reckon any rapid movement in the yen is more unfavourable than the yen's exchange value itself," he said. Any factors disrupting orderly moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be rectified, he added. \par \par \uc2  "As had been widely expected, the G7 offered nothing new on the exchange rate," said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dropped as low as about 117.85 yen on Friday in New York amid rumours that Tiger Management LP, the large hedge fund run by Julian Robertson, was having trouble meeting investor redemptions. \par \par \uc2  A spokesman for the fund later said that there was no substance to the rumour and that the fund had enough reserves to meet any redemption. \par \par \uc2  The spokesman also dismissed as untrue market rumours about a Federal Reserve-organised meeting to rescue to fund. \par \par \uc2  The rumours about Tiger reminded the markets of a sharp drop in the dollar against the yen last autumn triggered by a massive unwinding of yen carry trades by giant U.S. hedge fund Long-Term Capital Management, which was rescued from the brink of collapse. \par \par \uc2  "Speculation about a possible unwinding of yen carry trades by hedge funds could undermine confidence in the dollar," said a dealer at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  "Hedge-related selling by Japanese institutional investors is also likely to cap any dollar rebound," he added. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, the market would be watching the BOJ's policy board meeting, although no fresh policy moves were expected, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "With (Japan's) GDP and the G7 out of the way, the market will be watching U.S. and Japanese stock and bond markets for clues to dollar/yen direction," said a trust bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Japan's long-term interest rates rose sharply last week as gross domestic product data showed a robust 1.9 percent gain quarter-on-quarter in the January-March period, fuelling speculation that the BOJ would end its ultra-low interest rate policy sooner than previously expected. \par \par \uc2  But dealers agreed that speculation about possible BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to support the dollar near Thursday's Tokyo low of 117.63 yen. \par \par \uc2  Last Thursday, the BOJ stepped into the market to sell yen for dollars for the first time since January. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0499/02 at 2330 GMT, compared with $1.0528/33 in New York late on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the direction of the euro/dollar rate may be dictated by euro/yen movements during Asian trading hours. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 9780 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010907dv6d06kj7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
