\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Loses Ground On Japan Optimism \b0\par\par\uc2  By Arran Scott \par \uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 1999\par 07:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar lost ground against the yen in Asian trading Friday, as growing optimism toward Japan's economy encouraged market players to buy the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite more warnings from a senior Japanese financial official against an overly strong yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also edged down against the euro from its levels in New York late Thursday, as peace in Europe encouraged dealers to buy back the European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Early in the session, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  got a boost against its Japanese counterpart when Haruhiko Kuroda, the head of international bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gave fresh warnings against excessive yen strength, bringing back vivid memories of Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  "Now is a crucial time, and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability is extremely important. We're watching the markets and will take appropriate measures if necessary," Kuroda said. \par \par \uc2  The comments pushed the dollar to an intraday high of Y119.06. But the rise was limited as traders still dazzled by Thursday's data showing Japan's gross domestic product grew by a real 1.9% in the January-March quarter were reluctant to sell the yen. \par \par \uc2  "There has been a shift in sentiment regarding the Japanese economy." said Ken Landon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank in Tokyo. "The change in pace (of growth) is quite dramatic... and people are starting to wake up to that fact," Landon said. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (1:15 a.m. EDT), the dollar was quoted at Y118.75, below Y118.98 late Thursday in New York but unchanged from Y118.75 late Thursday in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0509, higher than $1.0480 late Thursday in New York and above $1.0486 in London Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 11-06-99 \par \par \uc2  0530GMT \par \par \uc2  8038 4162 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv6b04if0\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 17/10/1999\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\